\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"MS2500 / MV145 HV + lit. battery\", \"value\": {\"min\": 100, \"max\": 240}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"MS2500 / MV145 LLV + alk. battery\", \"value\": {\"min\": 10, \"max\": 48}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"MS2500 / MV145 LLV + lit. battery\", \"value\": {\"min\": 10, \"max\": 48}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n  ]\n}\n\npower_supply_type:\nAC / AC/DC / DC / AC / DC / DC\n\npower_supply_frequency:\n{min:45,max:66} Hz for HV(MV110), LV, HV(MV145); null others.\n\ninternal_backup_source:\nstrings as discussed.\n\nsoftware_version (axis \"electronics\"): MV110 → \"V.1.04.0005.0004\"; MV145 → \"V.1.05.0004.0005\"\ncrc_checksum: MV110 → \"9BA34F3B\"; MV145 → \"C96453B1\"\n\nratio config:\n{\n  \"attribute\": \"ratio_q3_over_q1\",\n  \"axis\": \"accuracy_class\",\n  \"values\": [{\"condition\": \"class 1\", \"value\": 250}, {\"condition\": \"class 2\", \"value\": 400}]\n}\n\nOK. Total config entries: ratio, mpe_lower, mpe_upper, q1, q2, max temp, temp class, ps voltage, ps type, ps frequency, backup source, sw version, crc = 13 entries. Good.\n\ntest_reports pages field: type_evaluation_report pages 381; others as listed. date only for TER: 2022-08-10.\n\nrevision_history: entries with revision \"0\" and \"1\" as strings.\n\nfootnotes: [] — omit (rule 8: omit if not present).\n\nLet me also double-check address: \"Okružní 31, 638 00 Brno, Czech Republic\" → address_lines: [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"Czech Republic\"].\n\nApplicant address: \"Via F.lli Gracchi, 27; Cinisello Balsamo; 20 099 Italy\" → [\"Via F.lli Gracchi, 27\", \"Cinisello Balsamo\", \"20 099 Italy\"].\n\nManufacturer: \"Via Piemonte 1, Montagnana – PD; PC: 350 44, Italy\" → [\"Via Piemonte 1\", \"Montagnana – PD\", \"350 44 Italy\"].\n\ncertified_type.description — compose from page 3.\n\nOne more consideration: certificate-level \"project_number\": none → omit.\n\nmember_state: \"Czech Republic\".\n\nscheme: \"A\".\n\nNow let me also think: should I include \"category\": \"Water meter\"? Schema examples: \"Gas meter\" — yes \"Water meter\" fits.\n\nWrite final JSON. Be careful with JSON validity: use \"≤\" and \"±\" characters — fine in JSON as UTF-8. Δp40, m³/h, °C — fine.\n\nLet me also make sure the type_level values structure: each is {\"value\": ..., \"unit_symbol\": ...}. Rule 2 says every characteristic value MUST be an object with value, unit_symbol, unit_id? It says shape with unit_symbol and unit_id... The example shape includes unit_id. \"Leave unit_id: null unless certain\". Should I include unit_id always? The example shape: {value, unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers}. To be safe include unit_id: null everywhere? That adds bulk. The rule says structured values strict with that shape; I'll include unit_symbol and set unit_id null only where unit present? Hmm. \"Leave unit_id: null unless you are certain of the unitsdb ID.\" I'll include unit_id: null on all entries for consistency. That's a lot of \"unit_id\": null. Acceptable.\n\nActually, let me reduce noise: include unit_id only alongside unit_symbol (i.e., when there is a unit). The shape shows footnote_markers optional too. I'll include unit_id: null everywhere a unit_symbol appears, and omit both when unit is null. Hmm, but shape requires unit_symbol: null? The example shape shows unit_symbol with null as possible. To be consistent I'll always include unit_symbol (null when none) and unit_id (null). Let me just always include: {\"value\": ..., \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null}. That's verbose but strictly conformant. Given the size of the response, I'll do it for type_level and per-value objects in model_level/config_level... that's a LOT of objects (13×5 + 26×2 + ...). Hmm.\n\nFor model_level values, the schema example in rules shows {\"model\": \"Emax=25t\", \"value\": 25} without unit (unit at attribute level: \"unit_symbol\": \"t\"). Yes! In rule 4 R60 example: model_level entry has attribute, unit_symbol, values[{model, value}]. So unit at attribute level for model_level. Good — compact.\n\nFor config_level, rule 5: \"Values follow the same structured form: {condition, value, unit_symbol}\" — I'll put unit_symbol per value only when non-null; attribute-level has no unit field per schema. Hmm, but then unit repeated per value. Alternatively put unit_symbol at the config_level entry level (like model_level)? The schema line: config_level[]: attribute, axis, values[]: {condition, value}. Rule 5 adds unit_symbol to the value form. I'll include unit_symbol per value only where there's a unit, omitting when null. Mixed but fine.\n\nFor type_level: include unit_symbol and unit_id. I'll include unit_id: null for entries with a unit_symbol. For dimensionless, unit_symbol null, unit_id null — include both? I'll include unit_id only when unit_symbol non-null. Actually simplest consistent: always include \"unit_symbol\" (null if none) and \"unit_id\" (null). Let me just do: every type_level object has value, unit_symbol, unit_id. And when footnote relevant, footnote_markers. No footnotes here.\n\nMatrix tables rows: raw values, no unit objects (units in column_units). Good.\n\nLet me now also decide on \"module_designation\" string. I'll write: \"MS2500 / MV110 HV; MS2500 / MV110 LV; MS2500 / MV110 LLV; MS2500 / MV145 HV + lit. battery; MS2500 / MV145 LLV + alk. battery; MS2500 / MV145 LLV + lit. battery\".\n\nDescription text:\n\n\"Electromagnetic water meter with electronic indicating device for measuring, memorising and displaying the volume of water passing through the measurement transducer at metering conditions. Consists of the sensor MS2500 and converter MV110 or MV145, in compact set-up or separate version with connecting cable. The sensor has a steel body with connecting flanges, one pair of excitation coils and electrodes, and is available with PTFE (DN25-DN350, up to 90 °C), polypropylene (DN25-DN150, 50 °C), Rilsan (DN50-DN350, 50 °C) or ebonite (DN200-DN350, 50 °C) liners. The converter comprises an LCD display showing volume and flow, impulse and current outputs, and non-legally relevant communication via RS485 or USB mini-B. Available in compact and separate versions; sealing by security seals and installation seals as described in Figures 1-4.\"\n\nGood.\n\nNow assemble everything. Watch JSON syntax carefully. Use standard quotes, no trailing commas.\n\nAlso: \"recommendation.scheme\": \"A\".\n\nLet me draft the final JSON.\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-2022.02\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"page_total\": 15,\n    \"member_state\": \"Czech Republic\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2022-09-13\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Czech Metrology Institute\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"Czech Republic\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"Jan Kalandra\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ISOIL INDUSTRIA SPA\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Via F.lli Gracchi, 27\", \"Cinisello Balsamo\", \"20 099 Italy\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Hemina SPA\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Via Piemonte 1\", \"Montagnana – PD\", \"350 44 Italy\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"MS2500 / MV110\", \"MS2500 / MV145\"],\n    \"module_designation\": \"MS2500 / MV110 HV; MS2500 / MV110 LV; MS2500 / MV110 LLV; MS2500 / MV145 HV + lit. battery; MS2500 / MV145 LLV + alk. battery; MS2500 / MV145 LLV + lit. battery\",\n    \"description\": \"...\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": null,\n    \"models\": [...]\n  },\n  \"components\": [...],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {...},\n    \"model_level\": [...],\n    \"config_level\": [...]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [...],\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R49\",\n    \"edition\": 2013,\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [1, 2]\n  },\n  \"test_reports\": [\n    